{
  "dom_id": "step-q61981",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "$({x}^{n}+3{y}^{n})({x}^{n}-3{y}^{n})=$",
  "worked_solution": "We will use the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n(a+b)(a-b)={a}^{2}-{b}^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a={x}^{n}$ and $b=3{y}^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{n}+3{y}^{n})({x}^{n}-3{y}^{n}) & = \\\\ {({x}^{n})}^{2}-(3{y}^{n})^{2} & = \\\\ {x}^{2n}-{3}^{2}\\cdot ({y}^{n})^{2} & = \\\\ {x}^{2n}-9{y}^{2n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
